Third-party attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------

KeysJoy  (https://github.com/iFeel-is-a-mouse/KeysJoy), Apache License 2.0

This project does NOT contain source code copied from KeysJoy. Its
repository was read while implementing the Android Bluetooth HID Device
transport, and the following API-usage details were taken from it as
prior art:

  * BluetoothAdapter.getProfileProxy(context, listener,
    BluetoothProfile.HID_DEVICE) as the entry point, and that the
    profile-proxy request can silently never call back on some ROMs.
  * The five-argument BluetoothHidDevice.registerApp(sdp, inQos, outQos,
    executor, callback) form, with the HID report descriptor passed as
    the descriptors argument of BluetoothHidDeviceAppSdpSettings and
    SUBCLASS1_COMBO used for a combined keyboard + mouse.
  * BluetoothHidDeviceAppQosSettings best-effort parameter values
    (800, 9, 0, 11250, MAX).
  * sendReport(device, reportId, payload) carrying a payload that does
    NOT include the report id byte.
  * Programmatic discoverability (BluetoothAdapter.setScanMode) is not
    available to third-party apps, so the ACTION_REQUEST_DISCOVERABLE
    system dialog has to be used instead.

Deliberate divergences from KeysJoy, for the record:

  * Its keyboard report descriptor declares a single key slot
    (Report Count 1). TouchDeck requires several keys held at once, so
    the descriptor here uses the standard boot-protocol layout with six
    key slots, written from scratch.
  * Report ids, the mouse collection (five buttons, 16-bit relative
    X/Y, vertical and horizontal wheel), the input state machine, the
    gesture recogniser, the touchpad engine, the layout model, the
    editor, the persistence layer, the Wi-Fi transport, the Windows
    receiver and all UI are original to this repository.
